@startuml possession-flow
' ⚠ RENDERING: this diagram is ~9,600px tall as of §3.14b, which is PAST
' PlantUML's default 4096px ceiling — `plantuml -tpng` SILENTLY TRUNCATES it
' to the top ~43% with no warning. Always render with:
'
'   plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng docs/possession-flow.puml
'
' `plantuml -checkonly` is unaffected (it parses, it does not lay out), so a
' green checkonly does NOT tell you the PNG is complete. Verify the rendered
' height if you add a partition.
title Possession Resolution (§3.2–§3.5, §3.7 blocks, §3.8 missed-shot OOB,\n§3.9 turnover causes, §3.10 rebounding fouls + bonus, §3.11 and-1,\n§3.12 all-shot-type contact fouls, §3.13 foul trouble, §3.14a technicals,\n§3.14b flagrants, §3.16 shooting-foul composition + charges,\n§3.17 shot mix / 3PA, §3.21 the rebound pool)

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start

note right
  **§3.4 coach pace** scales the possession COUNT
  (loop bound), blended across both coaches.
end note

partition "RotationState — between-possession sub (§3.5, §3.13, §3.14a)" {
  :drain on-floor energy (× endurance)
  recover benched energy;
  if (**§3.14a — technical foul?**\n//P = TECHNICAL_FOULS_PER_TEAM_GAME ÷ nominal checks//\nrolled PER TEAM, no causal model at all) then (yes)
    :FOUL — TECHNICAL_FOUL
    committer: //foulProne//-weighted draw
    over the ON-FLOOR FIVE only;
    :**1 free throw** to the other team
    shooter = highest //freeThrows// on the floor
    (DETERMINISTIC — consumes no RNG);
    note right
      **§3.14a (#032 B/C/D/E/G) — the foul with NO contest behind it.**
      Every other foul in this engine is a by-product of a contest
      (pickDefender → isFoul). A technical is **behavioral**, so it
      hangs off nothing — which is exactly why it is rolled HERE,
      between possessions, and **NOT** on the possession path.
      **THE POSSESSION IS UNCHANGED** (D) — no fork, no retention,
      no switch, even when the offense commits it. §3.14a adds
      **NO branch below this partition**; if you are looking for one,
      there isn't one, and that is the design.
      **Its own counter** (E): does NOT feed FOUL_OUT_LIMIT, does NOT
      feed foulTroubleLevel(), and is EXCLUDED from the period bonus
      tally — #028 A1's first outcome-aware exception.
      **Committer is on-floor only** (C): the bench is excluded to
      avoid spending ~2/3 of the rate on players whose technicals
      have no engine consequence. foulProne is nearly flat (sd 1.22),
      so the draw is near-uniform — accepted, because the RATE is a
      fixed constant and the weighting moves no aggregate.
      **No PROB_FLOOR** (H): the floor (0.02) is more than **10×**
      the per-check rate (**~0.00175**) — it would inflate technicals
      by that factor. Routed through the shared floor-free clamp
      helper (`clampRareProbability`) this pass added.
      //Execution correction: #032 B2 estimated the per-check rate at//
      //~0.0035 off ~100 checks per team-game. The true count is ~200 —//
      //BOTH rotations advance on EVERY possession — so the rate is half//
      //that. The game-level constant (0.35) is unchanged.//
      //The roll and committer draw live in RotationState; the EVENT and//
      //the FT are emitted by PossessionEngine, which owns GameData, the//
      //team ids, the period and the sequence. advancePossession returns//
      //the committer.//
    end note
  else (no)
  endif
  :**hard** — force off any fouled-out OR ejected player
  //isFouledOut() || isEjected() || isEjectedForFlagrant()//
  //(fouls >= 6 · technicalFouls >= 2 · flagrantTwos >= 1)//
  → sub from full roster;
  :**soft** — foul-trouble sub (§3.13)
  //P = base(fouls) × subAggressiveness × value × roster//
  from //rotationDepth// window only; yields if bench can't cover;
  :fatigue sub — pull most-tired starter below
  //subAggressiveness// threshold for freshest bench
  within //rotationDepth//; starters pulled later / return first;
  note right
    Three tiers: **hard/forced · soft/preference · fatigue**
    (#031 H). **§3.14a's ejection extends the HARD tier via
    the `eligible(...)` filter — NOT a fourth removal path.**
    It stays **DERIVED** (//technicalFouls >= 2//, a monotonic
    counter — #023 F applies unchanged, #032 F).
    **§3.14b adds a THIRD cause to the SAME predicate**
    (//flagrantTwos >= 1//) — still not a fourth path, and
    still **DERIVED**. #031 H / #032 F predicted a flagrant-2
    would finally force stored state; **it does not** (#034 F):
    a flagrant-2 ejects IMMEDIATELY, so there is no threshold
    to remember and the counter is monotonic like the other
    two. **Every disqualification here is absorbing — which
    is exactly the shape #023 F's derivation was built for.
    The stored-state prediction is RETIRED, not deferred.**
    Flagrant ejections land ~0.024/team/game — roughly DOUBLE
    §3.14a's 0.014, so this tier is finally exercised.
    **Consumes THREE RNG draws** — §3.13's sit roll, §3.14a's
    technical roll, and §3.14a's committer draw, ALL taken
    unconditionally at fixed points so the stream never forks
    on rotation state (decisions.md #031, revising #023 C's
    RNG-free sub). The committer draw is drawn even on the
    ~99.8% of calls that don't need it, precisely to keep the
    count state-independent. //(Execution: THREE, not the TWO//
    //the design pass drew — the committer draw was made//
    //unconditional for the same fixed-point reason.)//
    The step itself emits no events: it RETURNS the technical's
    committer and PossessionEngine emits the FOUL + free throw.
    The soft rule protects the BEST players MORE — the
    deliberate inverse of the fatigue rule's starter
    tolerance. Sticky sit: return is EARNED via the
    fatigue freshness path, never re-rolled.
    onFloor() is always exactly 5 (least-fouled stays
    as last resort). A fouled-out player NEVER returns.
  end note
}

repeat
:ShotSelector
  pick shooter (offensive-weight draw)
  pick shot type (**§3.17 — per-type SHARE table × avg-10 skill modifier**
  //DRIVE / PERIMETER / POST / THREE, sim.shot-share-* (#040 C)//
  //THREE × offensiveScheme lean · PERIMETER × its RECIPROCAL (#040 D)//);
note right
  **§3.17 (decisions.md #040 A/C/D/E) — THE SHOT MIX, and the only
  place in this engine where the LEAGUE's shot distribution is set.**
  **No new branch and no new RNG draw** — `pickShotType` still takes
  exactly one `nextDouble()` and still returns one of four types. What
  §3.17 changes is how the four WEIGHTS are computed, which is why this
  is a node and not a fork. It nonetheless moves nearly every possession.
  **The cause it fixes** (A/B): `shotTypeWeight` gave **DRIVE the SUM of
  two skills** (`drive + finishing`) while the other three got one each,
  so at an average player — which every SkillCalculator is built to
  produce — the draw was **DRIVE 40 · PER 20 · POST 20 · THREE 20**.
  Measured draw share 20.9% against a real **41.5%**. Not the player
  population: an artifact of #021 D naming **five** skills for **four**
  shot types, argued nowhere. The accuracy path `offenseSkillForShot`
  averages the same two skills and is **CORRECT and UNTOUCHED** — 3P%
  is 37.8 vs a sourced 36.0. **This pass changes how OFTEN a three is
  taken, never how often it goes in.**
  **The lean SPLITS** (D): `shotMixLean` used to scale PERIMETER and
  THREE **together**, so it could not raise threes while lowering
  mid-range — #036 D's named blocker. THREE now takes the lean and
  PERIMETER takes its **reciprocal**, which is the actual
  modern-vs-traditional axis. `CoachModifiers` is unchanged.
  ⚠ **THIS PASS DOES NOT HOLD FGA — the opposite of a §3.9/§3.16
  re-partition, and #040 E's central finding.** A stopped shot charges
  **no FGA** (the foul branch below returns before recordFieldGoalAttempt),
  and `foul-mult-three` is **0.133** against DRIVE's **1.0** — so a draw
  moved to a three is **7.5× less likely to be stopped** and more likely
  to become a charged attempt. **SHIPPED: FGA 88.80 -> 92.28**, past its
  sourced 89.1 — the mechanism was right, the magnitude was
  under-modelled (~89.9 predicted). **#039 C's dead-possession
  concession is therefore NOT revisitable here** — it passes to §3.20.
  ⚠ **FG% fell 46.68 -> 43.52 and that was §3.20's, not drift** (F) — ✅ **CLOSED:
  §3.20 landed FG% 46.86 and 2P% 54.67 (#042).** The reasoning below stands: the
  engine's **2P% is ~48.7 against a real 55.0**, an error the old
  two-heavy mix HID because FG% ~= 2P% at a 21% three share. §3.17 makes
  the shape final; §3.20 re-solves `base-drive`/`base-post`/
  `base-perimeter`. ⚠ **`base-three` must NOT move** — 3P% is 35.8 vs a
  sourced 36.0 and it HELD across a 1.9x volume change.
  ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08: 3PA 19.96 -> 37.22** (target 37.0) at shares
  **1.0 / 0.55 / 0.55 / 1.23**; charged three share 40.3% vs a real
  41.5%. **The lean split was measured separately and moved 3PA by
  ZERO**, exactly as D predicted — it is a per-coach lever, not a
  volume lever.
  ⚠ **BLOCKS DID NOT FALL as #040 E predicted (~2.6); they stayed at
  4.80.** `PROB_FLOOR` (0.02) is **4x `base-block-three` (0.005)**, so a
  three's block chance is FLOORED, not based — `base-block-three` is
  currently INERT. A §3.20 finding, not a §3.17 miss.
end note

partition "TurnoverResolver (§3.9 causes — decisions.md #027)" {
  if (turnover?\n//ballSecurity vs stealing/individualDefense//\n//× defensiveScheme pressure §3.4//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    note right
      **The gate above is UNCHANGED by §3.9** (#027 A) — a turnover
      happens exactly as often as before. Only AFTER a turnover is
      declared does a weighted draw pick WHICH of NINE causes it was,
      so the draw re-partitions the label without moving the count.
      That is what made §3.9 free by construction.
      Leans (#027 C): SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION on //acumen//↓ ×
      //defensiveScheme//↑; OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS on //teamOffense//↓.
      STOLEN stays dominant. Every cause charges the ball-handler.
    end note
    if (cause == STOLEN?\n//weighted nine-way draw//) then (yes)
      :TURNOVER — STOLEN
      primaryPlayerId = the ball-handler (the victim)
      **opponentPlayerId = the STEALER** //(§3.18 — #041 A/B)//
      stealer.recordSteal() — the box-score credit, unchanged;
      note right
        **§3.18 (#041 A/B): the stealer now lands ON THE EVENT.**
        Until §3.18 pickStealer chose them, recordSteal() credited
        them, and the engine then DROPPED them — making the steal the
        last contested defensive play the log could not attribute.
        ONE row, not two: no PlayType.STEAL and no second event
        (#041 B). The rule that decides it (#041 C): **second
        PARTICIPANT -> a column; second ACCOUNTING -> an event;
        neither -> nothing.** A steal has a participant, so it takes
        the column; the charge below has an accounting consequence a
        column cannot carry (isInBonus counts FOUL EVENTS), so it
        keeps its two events.
        ⚠ **NO NEW DRAW.** Only the declaration was hoisted so the
        value reaches addEvent — pickStealer runs at the same point
        in the stream, so §3.18 moves NO number. Same at the two
        other counterparty sites (BLOCKED_*, SHOOTING_FOUL).
        Buys the PER-CREDITOR reconciliation (#041 G):
        count(STOLEN with opponent = X) == box_score.steals(X), forall X
        — the old TOTAL check passed even on a wrong-player bug.
      end note
    else (no)
      :TURNOVER — one of
      SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION / OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS /
      TRAVELLING / LOST_BALL_OUT_OF_BOUNDS / 3_SECONDS_VIOLATION /
      8_SECONDS_BACKCOURT_VIOLATION / OVER_AND_BACK
      //no stealer credited//;
      note right
        ⚠ **§3.18: opponentPlayerId is NULL on all eight of these,
        and that is a DECISION, not an omission.** Seven have one
        actor and no counterparty at all, so nothing is owed
        (#041 C). OFFENSIVE_FOUL is the exception worth naming: a
        charge HAS a real counterparty — the defender who drew it —
        and the engine **never picks one**. Populating it needs a
        NEW pickChargeDrawer draw, which would shift the stream and
        re-baseline every seeded sim test, forfeiting §3.18's
        "moves no number" property for a participant nothing
        consumes. Parked as an #041 follow-up.
      end note
      if (**§3.16 — cause == OFFENSIVE_FOUL?**\n//the charge / illegal screen — a PERSONAL FOUL by rule//) then (yes)
        :FOUL — OFFENSIVE_FOUL
        charge the BALL-HANDLER //recordFoul()// (G)
        committingTeamId = **OFFENSE** — so the DEFENSE gains the bonus;
        note right
          **§3.16 (decisions.md #039 G) — the charge correctness fix (#037).**
          ⚠ **TWO EVENTS FOR ONE OCCURRENCE**: the TURNOVER above and this
          FOUL both describe the same charge. Any reconciliation that counts
          events must tolerate that, and the harness's ``Fouls / team / game``
          line steps up **~1.26 for this reason alone** — NOT the §3.16
          re-partition misfiring.
          Before §3.16 ``recordFoul()`` was **never called** here, so a charge
          counted toward nothing: not the committer's six, not the team-foul
          tally, not the box-score ``fouls`` column (#027 never considered it).
          **This is the ONLY site where the committer is on OFFENSE outside the
          rebounding foul**, so it is the only other path that puts the
          DEFENSIVE team in the bonus. ``GameData.isInBonus`` reads
          ``committingTeamId`` and already supports it.
          **NOT flagrant-eligible** (#039 G) — the flagrant roll lives in
          FoulResolver and this path never reaches it. Counts toward the
          bonus and FOUL_OUT_LIMIT: it is a personal foul.
          The possession already ends (it is a turnover), so #039 C's
          possession question does not arise here.
        end note
      endif
    endif
    stop
  endif
}

partition "FoulResolver" {
  note right
    **§3.12 (decisions.md #030 A1/A2) — SHIPPED.**
    The binary ``ShotType.isContactType()`` gate that stood here
    (DRIVE or POST?) is **DELETED**. **Every** shot type can now be
    fouled, graduated by a per-shot-type multiplier on the base
    constant: DRIVE 1.0 (the anchor) ≈ POST > PERIMETER > THREE.
    That base is **UNTOUCHED at 0.15** and still means "P(contact
    stops the shot)" **on a drive**, so drive/post rates stay
    numerically identical to §3.11 and the whole §3.12 delta is
    attributable to the two newly foulable types (A2).
    It is **RENAMED ``BASE_FOUL`` → ``BASE_NO_BASKET_FOUL``** (F) —
    value unchanged; it never meant "the foul rate", it means the
    foul STOPPED the shot, which is exactly why trimming it moves
    points the WRONG way (see the legend).
    A multiplier of 0.0 — not a zero base — is the only true
    off-switch (the #029 zero-base finding).
  end note
  if (foul?\n//foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× foulMultiplier(shotType) §3.12 A1//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :**defender.recordFoul()** — the foul is CHARGED here
    //NO event is emitted yet — the two rolls below decide WHICH//
    //foul event this becomes. Exactly ONE is ever emitted (#039 A),//
    //and the charge is what holds the foul TOTAL by construction//;
    note right
      foul rate × defensiveScheme pressure §3.4.
      This is the **pre-shot** foul — the shot is stopped,
      a 2-FT trip (**3 on a THREE**, §3.12 C), mutually
      exclusive with a made basket. The **and-1** (foul WITH
      a made shot) is a separate post-make roll (§3.11,
      inside SHOT — MADE below).
      **NB the stopped shot charges NO FGA** — this branch
      returns before recordFieldGoalAttempt() — so it removes
      points without moving FG% directly, but it DOES change
      the shot mix FG% is computed over (§3.12 E).
      ⚠ **READ THE THREE-WAY SHAPE BELOW CAREFULLY — it is ONE
      foul with THREE possible labels, not three fouls.**
      ``recordFoul()`` has ALREADY run above, so neither roll
      below moves the foul RATE; they only decide the outcome
      STRING and what free throws follow. **SHOOTING_FOUL is the
      FALL-THROUGH** — the label a foul gets when both rolls miss,
      which is why it appears LAST here even though it is the
      most common. A flagrant **REPLACES** it (#034 C); a
      non-shooting foul **REPLACES** it (#039 A). They never compose.
    end note

    if (**§3.14b — FLAGRANT?**\n//P = FLAGRANT_FOULS_PER_TEAM_GAME ÷ personal fouls//\n//layered ON TOP of the foul — no rate re-partitioned//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
      //15% severity sub-roll (#034 E) — flat, no causal input//
      charge committer //recordFoul()// — a PERSONAL foul (I)
      on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
      :FREE_THROW ×**2** — *_FLAGRANT (new source)
      the FOULED player shoots (D)
      **REPLACES the 2/3 FTs above — does NOT add** (C);
      note right
        **§3.14b (#034 A/B/C) — THE POSSESSION-RETENTION FORK,
        and the first FT path in this engine that does NOT end
        the possession** (breaking #030 B's invariant).
        A defensive flagrant returns the ball: the offense
        **RE-ENTERS the second-chance loop** — the SAME
        ``offensiveRebounds++; continue;`` §3.7/§3.8/§3.10 use,
        under the SAME MAX_OFFENSIVE_RETENTIONS cap (B). No new
        mechanism: the loop already IS "same team, run it again".
        This site is **always defensive**, so it always retains.
        ⚠ **The terminator below is NOT "possession over"** — it is where
        this branch leaves the diagram to re-enter the loop at ShotSelector.
        Activity-diagram syntax cannot draw an edge back into the enclosing
        ``repeat`` from inside a partition, so retention is shown as the
        labelled step above rather than as a drawn arrow. **Every other
        ``stop`` on this page really does end the possession; these three
        flagrant ones do not.**
      end note
      :→ **OFFENSE RETAINS** → ``offensiveRebounds++; continue;``
      re-enter the second-chance loop at ShotSelector (B)
      //(unless the cap is already reached — then the possession ends,//
      //the FTs having been awarded either way, exactly as §3.10 degrades)//;
      stop
    endif

    if (**§3.16 — NON-SHOOTING FOUL?**\n//flat sim.non-shooting-foul-share, NO skill input (#039 E)//\n//a SECOND roll on the foul already charged above//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — **NON_SHOOTING_FOUL** //(§3.17 renamed it from COMMON_FOUL, #040 M)//
      //the foul was ALREADY charged above — this only re-labels it//
      counts toward the bonus AND FOUL_OUT_LIMIT (B);
      note right
        **§3.16 (decisions.md #039 A/B/C/D) — THE FTA RE-PARTITION,
        and the whole point of the phase.**
        **Layered, not carved** — the ``isFoul`` roll above is UNCHANGED
        in rate, skills and RNG draw, and ``recordFoul()`` has already
        run, so **the foul TOTAL holds by construction** (A). Exactly the
        ``isFlagrant`` shape three lines up (#034 A) and §3.9's turnover
        causes one layer out (#027 A).
        **Order matters**: flagrant is rolled FIRST, so a flagrant common
        foul is simply a flagrant (F) — the two never compose.
        ⚠ **THE POSSESSION ENDS AND THE BALL DOES NOT COME BACK (C), AND
        THAT IS DELIBERATELY WRONG AS BASKETBALL.** A real common foul is
        a side inbound: the offense keeps the ball. It is not modelled
        that way because **every returning variant yields a live attempt
        worth ~0.76 FGA where the stopped shot charged NONE**, and FGA is
        88.4 against 89.1 real — **0.7 of headroom**. That caps a
        retaining variant at a **~6% share**, which moves FTA by less
        than 1.0. The retention reading and the phase goal are
        arithmetically incompatible; FGA wins because it is sourced and
        already correct.
        **Share 0.50, and it is BACK-SOLVED, NOT SOURCED (D)** — the real
        NBA shooting-foul share is not in a league-averages row. The
        earlier ~35% figure is **withdrawn**: it assumed zero FTs, but a
        large share of these fouls are committed **ALREADY IN THE PENALTY**
        and those award 2 bonus FTs. #039 D predicted 0.43 from an 18.5%
        in-penalty share; the charge fork above raised the bonus rate to
        ~56% of team-periods, so each conversion removes ~1.47 FTs and the
        share measured out at **0.50** (5 seeds, FTA 23.6). The LANDING is
        the target, not the constant.
        ⚠ **Points falls ~8 to ~110 and §3.20 RECOVERS IT (H)** — not
        drift, and NOT to be chased here (#038's rule).
      end note
      if (committing team already in the penalty?\n//GameData.isInBonus — emit-then-count, §3.10 #028 A1//) then (yes)
        :FREE_THROW ×**2** — BONUS
        //the fouled team shoots; this is the 18.5% case above//;
      else (no)
        :**no free throws** — the point of the phase;
      endif
      stop
    endif

    :FOUL — **SHOOTING_FOUL** //— THE FALL-THROUGH: both rolls above missed//
    //the same already-charged foul; this is just the label it keeps//
    primaryPlayerId = the DEFENDER who committed it; committingTeamId = defense
    **opponentPlayerId = the FOULED SHOOTER** //(§3.18 — #041 A)//;
    note right
      ⚠ **The counterparty's ORIENTATION FLIPS here relative to the
      steal and the block, and the invariant still holds.** At those
      two, primary is the victim and the opponent is the defender who
      acted. Here primary is the COMMITTER, so the opponent is on
      OFFENSE. That is exactly why #041 A defines the column as "the
      other side of the play" rather than "the defender": the rule
      that survives every site is **opponent is ALWAYS the opposite
      team from primary** — so a reader resolves their team without
      decoding the outcome string. No new draw: `shooter` was already
      in scope. A teammate never goes here (an assister rides
      assistPlayerId, #041 D).
      ⚠ **The SWEEP (#041 addendum): opponentPlayerId is populated wherever a
      real contest identified an INDIVIDUAL victim — SHOOTING_FOUL,
      NON_SHOOTING_FOUL, AND_ONE, and FLAGRANT_* at the two SHOT sites.**
      It is NULL BY CONTRACT at the REBOUNDING site: that foul is committed
      against the TEAM contesting the board and no individual victim is ever
      identified. Its FT shooter is a foulDrawing-weighted DRAW standing in
      for the award, so populating from it would attribute the foul to a
      player the engine never decided was fouled.
      ⚠ Also pinned by test, previously true by inspection only: on EVERY
      FOUL event primaryPlayerId is the COMMITTER (the player charged
      recordFoul(), on committingTeamId) — the inverse of SHOT/TURNOVER,
      where primary is the victim.
    end note
    repeat
      if (free throw made?\n//freeThrows skill//) then (yes)
        :FREE_THROW — MADE_SHOOTING (source-tagged §3.11 D)
        +1 point;
      else (no)
        :FREE_THROW — MISSED_SHOOTING;
      endif
    repeat while (shotType.freeThrowsIfFouled() done?\n//§3.12 C: 3 for THREE, else 2//) is (no) not (yes)
    note right
      **§3.12 C — the latent fouled-three fix.** The count is a
      RULE on ShotType (``freeThrowsIfFouled()``), not a SimConfig
      tunable, threaded through #029 D's already-parameterized
      ``awardFreeThrows`` — a call-site change, no new plumbing.
      A stopped THREE = **3** FTs; it never fired before only
      because THREE wasn't a contact type. No new FreeThrowSource:
      these are SHOOTING FTs, there are simply three of them.
      **§3.14b (#034 C): if this foul turned FLAGRANT the count
      becomes a flat 2 — so a flagrant stopped THREE awards FEWER
      FTs than the ordinary foul it upgraded. Correct by rule,
      counter-intuitive, and NOT to be "fixed" into 3 + 2.**
    end note

    partition "Missed LAST free throw → live rebound (§3.21 — #043 C/D)" {
      note right
        ⚠ **DRAWN ONCE HERE, BUT IT APPLIES AT THREE SOURCES** —
        ``SHOOTING`` (this loop), ``BONUS`` and ``AND_ONE``. It lives in
        ``awardFreeThrows``, which all three share, so one fork serves all
        three. **Do not draw it three times.**
        ⚠ **IN CODE THIS IS A SECOND LAYER, NOT A BRANCH INSIDE THE SHARED
        TRIP (#043 H).** ``awardFreeThrows`` keeps owning the shared trip
        (attempt, make roll, score, emit) and its ``int`` return, unchanged;
        a new ``awardLiveFreeThrows`` wraps it and adds the board, returning
        ``FreeThrowResult(sequence, offenseRetains)``. ⚠ **FLAGRANT and
        TECHNICAL are NOT flagged off — they simply never call the wrapper**,
        because their possession consequence is fixed BY RULE and independent
        of the FT outcome. **That is why they are absent from this fork
        rather than drawn as a "no" leg.**
        ⚠ **AND_ONE turns its caller's ``return`` into a ``continue`` — a
        live second-chance possession AFTER a made basket, reversing
        #029 B**, exactly as #034 B's flagrant and-1 already does.
        **Read #043 H before building.**

        **Until §3.21 there was NO rebound path here at all** —
        ``awardFreeThrows`` looped, emitted and returned, so a missed final
        FT silently ended the possession. **~2.64/team-game.** By rule the
        last FT of a trip is live and someone rebounds it.

        ⚠ **ONLY THE LAST ATTEMPT IS LIVE.** A missed FIRST FT is a dead
        ball. Measured, non-last misses are **2.30/team-game — LARGER than
        the live ones**, so the terminal test (``ft == count - 1``) is the
        whole correctness of this branch.

        ⚠ **TWO SOURCES ARE EXCLUDED BY RULE, and building it uniformly
        would be WRONG:** ``FLAGRANT`` — the offense RETAINS the ball
        (#034 B, already modelled; rebounding it would double-count that
        path) — and ``TECHNICAL`` — play resumes with the ball as it was
        (#032 G). Together only 0.10/team-game, so exclusion costs nothing.

        ⚠ **The contest is the ORDINARY board contest at a REDUCED base**
        (``baseOffensiveRebound() × FREE_THROW_REBOUND_LEAN``): the defense
        has inside position **by rule**, so the realized offensive share is
        ~**0.19**, not the board's 0.262. ``FREE_THROW_REBOUND_LEAN`` is a
        ``public static final`` **RULE constant, NOT a tunable** — §3.20
        held at **62 tunables**; statics move 27 → **28**.
      end note
      if (last FT of the trip, AND missed?
//source is SHOOTING / BONUS / AND_ONE only//) then (yes)
        :resolve through **MissedShotResolver** //(reused WHOLE — #026 B)//
        base = baseOffensiveRebound() × FREE_THROW_REBOUND_LEAN
        → REBOUND — OFFENSIVE / DEFENSIVE / OUT_OF_BOUNDS_*;
        note right
          **Reused whole, not reimplemented** — the OOB carve, the cap
          forcing and the credit path all come for free. ~7% of FT
          rebounds resolve ``OUT_OF_BOUNDS_*``; that is a real outcome
          on a missed free throw, not a defect.

          ⚠ **An OFFENSIVE rebound here RETURNS THE BALL** → the same
          ``continue`` shape the offensive rebound and #034 B's flagrant
          already use, under the SAME cap. ⚠ **The fork stays at the CALL
          SITES**, but the FACT comes from ``awardLiveFreeThrows``, which
          returns ``FreeThrowResult(sequence, offenseRetains)`` (#043 H —
          this supersedes an earlier reading that ``awardFreeThrows`` itself
          returns only a sequence; **it still does**, and that is exactly
          why the second layer exists).
        end note
        stop
      else (no — dead ball, or an excluded source)
      endif
    }
    stop
  endif
}

partition "ShotResolver" {
  :record FGA (+ 3PA if THREE);

  if (BLOCKED? //§3.7 — decisions.md #025//\n//P(BLOCK) carved off the top (A1), then MAKE/MISS on remainder//\n//contest: defender rimProtection (rim) / shotContest (jumper)//\n//vs shooter finishing (B2); own BLOCK_SENSITIVITY, THREE very-low (C)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :SHOT — BLOCKED_*
    event: PlayType.SHOT, outcome BLOCKED_* (F1)
    primaryPlayerId = shooter (the victim)
    **opponentPlayerId = the BLOCKER** //(§3.18 — #041 A, closing #025 F2)//
    shooter charged missed FGA (+3PA if THREE), 0 FGM (F3)
    blocker.recordBlock() — the box-score credit, unchanged
    no assistPlayerId (F4);
    note right
      **Block = a field-goal outcome, exactly as a steal is a
      turnover outcome** (§3.2: TURNOVER/STOLEN + recordSteal).
      v3: one three-way MAKE/MISS/BLOCK draw — no double-count
      (probs sum to 1). No new PlayType.BLOCK. Reconciliation:
      count(SHOT outcome LIKE 'BLOCKED%') == sum(BoxScore.blocks).
      ⚠ **§3.18 (#041 A) closed F2, and the symmetry above is WHY it
      had to be closed twice.** F2 left the blocker off the event BY
      DESIGN, "mirroring the stealer" — so §3.7 copied the gap
      rather than closing it, and #027 A carried it forward. Each
      call was locally right and the whole drifted. The blocker now
      rides opponentPlayerId (no new draw — `defender` was already
      selected), which upgrades the line above to the PER-CREDITOR
      form: count(BLOCKED% with opponent = X) == blocks(X), forall X.
    end note

    partition "BlockResolver (§3.7 — #025 D; §3.21 credits — #043 E)" {
      note right
        A blocked ball is a **chaotic loose ball**, NOT the
        offenseRebound-vs-defenseRebound box-out contest — so
        recovery is a FLAT four-way roll (fixed weights, same
        for every block, defense-leaning). Weights are
        placeholders → calibrate empirically (~5 blocks/team).

        ⚠ **§3.21 (#043 E) — THE FLAT ROLL PICKS A SIDE, NEVER A
        PLAYER, and that is why the credit below does NOT violate
        #025 D.** Until §3.21 the two IN-BOUNDS cases emitted
        **nothing** — 3.40/team-game where a player demonstrably
        secured the ball and was credited to nobody. By the NBA rule
        that is a rebound. **Two different questions:** *which side*
        stays this flat roll (unchanged), *which of that side's five*
        is a new skill-weighted pick. ⚠ **isOffensiveRebound() is
        NEVER called here** — the side is already decided, and running
        the board contest would be exactly the inheritance #025 D
        refused. ⚠ **The possession fork is UNCHANGED** (offenseRetains()
        already drove it correctly): this adds a credit + an event
        BEFORE the fork. ⚠ **Consumes a new RNG draw** — seeded sim
        tests re-baseline (#043 E3).

        ⚠ **READ THIS BRANCH COLD AND COUNT THE EVENTS: a block now
        emits TWO, and that is correct.** Before §3.21 it emitted exactly
        one (the ``SHOT — BLOCKED_*`` above) and this partition emitted
        none. It is now ``SHOT`` **then** ``REBOUND``, one of each, on
        every one of the four cases — the switch below is four MUTUALLY
        EXCLUSIVE cases, not four events. That is the §3.14b/§3.16 failure
        mode inverted: there the boxes claimed three events where the
        engine emitted one; here the count genuinely moved from one to
        two, so the picture had to GAIN a node rather than lose one.
        ⚠ **The block reconciliation is unaffected** — it counts
        ``SHOT`` events with a ``BLOCKED%`` outcome, and this pass emits
        no new ``SHOT`` event anywhere.
      end note
      switch (recovery? //flat four-way roll (D) — picks the SIDE only//)
      case (RECOVERED_OFFENSE)
        :**REBOUND — OFFENSIVE** //(§3.21 — #043 E)//
        pickOffensiveRebounder(offense) — skill-weighted
        recordOffensiveRebound()
        in-bounds, offense retains
        → second-chance (respects the cap);
        stop
      case (RECOVERED_DEFENSE)
        :**REBOUND — DEFENSIVE** //(§3.21 — #043 E)//
        pickDefensiveRebounder(defense) — skill-weighted
        recordDefensiveRebound()
        in-bounds, defense's ball
        → possession over;
        stop
      case (OOB_OFFENSE)
        :**REBOUND — OUT_OF_BOUNDS_OFFENSE** //(§3.21 — #043 E2)//
        no rebounder (primaryPlayerId null)
        OOB off the blocker
        → offense retains → second-chance;
        stop
      case (OOB_DEFENSE)
        :**REBOUND — OUT_OF_BOUNDS_DEFENSE** //(§3.21 — #043 E2)//
        no rebounder (primaryPlayerId null)
        OOB off the shooter
        → defense's ball → possession over;
        stop
      endswitch
      note right
        **§3.21 E2 — the two OOB slices gain their EVENT, not a
        rebounder** (1.13/team-game). Same shape ``emitMissedShotEvent``
        already uses off a missed shot, so the derived team-rebound
        query — ``count(REBOUND where outcome LIKE 'OUT_OF_BOUNDS%')`` —
        is finally **complete**. ⚠ This is why the ``teamRebounds``
        COLUMN still is not built: nothing consumes it and it stays
        derivable (#014/#017/#020).
      end note
    }
  else (no)
    if (shot made?\n//offense skill vs defense skill//\n//× acumen + teamOffense/teamDefense §3.4//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
      :SHOT — MADE_*
      +2 or +3 points;
      partition "Assist (§3.4)" {
        if (assisted?\n//supporting-cast passing draw//) then (yes)
          :stamp assist_player_id
          credit assister;
        endif
      }
      partition "And-1 (§3.11 — decisions.md #029)" {
        note right
          **And-1 = a SECOND, post-make foul roll** (A1), carved
          BESIDE the assist — the pre-shot foul branch + BASE_FOUL
          are untouched, so this rate is independently tunable
          (the §3.7 block / §3.10 rebound-foul carve, a third time).
          A made basket already ended the possession → the and-1
          NEVER forks it; it only tacks on ONE FT (B). Coexists with
          the assist, doesn't interact (A3). Rate = rareEventProbability
          on AND_ONE_BASE + its own AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY (C).
        end note
        note right
          **§3.12 (decisions.md #030 A1/B) — SHIPPED.**
          §3.11's ``DRIVE or POST?`` gate here is **DELETED** — every
          made shot now rolls the and-1, and the graduation lives in
          the rate via the **SAME shared** foulMultiplier(shotType)
          table the pre-shot roll uses (B: one table, not two — the
          contact propensity is a property of the SHOT, not of which
          roll is asking). An and-1 on a THREE is rarer than a foul
          on a three **automatically**: the two rolls are independent
          and the shot must ALSO go in, so modeling it again would
          double-count it.
          **The two foul rolls are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE** — trace the
          flow above: the pre-shot FoulResolver branch **stops**, so a
          stopped shot never reaches here. One shot emits at most ONE
          of SHOOTING_FOUL / AND_ONE, never both, and the shared table
          is never applied twice to the same shot. The and-1 is
          conditioned TWICE (survived the foul roll, AND went in), so
          at §3.11's numbers a drive is ~15% stopped + ~2.6% and-1 —
          **~17.6% combined, not double**. Where they DO compound is
          the §3.10 period foul tally: both emit a FOUL and both count
          toward the bonus (and-1s alone moved fouls 3.95 → 4.41/team/
          period in §3.11). §3.12 roughly DOUBLES this roll's REACH
          — every made shot, not just made DRIVE/POST — but **MEASURED,
          the and-1 RATE rose only ~1.12× (1.67 → 1.87/team/game)**,
          because the shared multiplier lands TWICE in this path and
          compounds with the lower make rates. The tally channel is
          what the penalty-rate line (D) watches: 43.4% → 52.3% of
          team-periods in the penalty.
        end note
        if (and-1?\n//shooter foulDrawing vs defender discipline//\n//× foulMultiplier(shotType) §3.12 B — same table//\n//× defensivePressure; AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY (C)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
          if (**§3.14b — FLAGRANT?**\n//same shared roll (#034 A)//) then (yes)
            :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
            //15% severity sub-roll//; charge defender //recordFoul()//
            on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
            :FREE_THROW ×**2** — *_FLAGRANT
            the SHOOTER shoots (he was fouled, D)
            **2, not the and-1's 1 — replaces, doesn't add** (C);
            :**BASKET COUNTS + 2 FTs + OFFENSE RETAINS**
            → ``offensiveRebounds++; continue;`` (B)
            //(cap reached ⇒ possession ends, FTs still awarded)//
            **the ``stop`` below means "re-enters the loop", NOT "over"**;
            note right
              **THE CASE THAT MOST VISIBLY BREAKS #030 B** (#034 C).
              THREE scoring channels on ONE possession — the made FG,
              two free throws, AND the ball back. No other path in
              this engine produces that, it looks exactly like a
              double-count bug in a play-by-play, and **it is the
              rule**. #029 B's "the and-1 NEVER forks the possession —
              the make already ended it" is **superseded for the
              FLAGRANT case only**; the ordinary and-1 below is
              completely unchanged.
            end note
            stop
          endif
          :FOUL — AND_ONE
          charge defender foul (feeds foul-outs + §3.10 tally)
          committing_team_id = defTeamId (reuses #028 D column);
          :FREE_THROW — *_AND_ONE (source-tagged, D)
          ONE FT for the shooter (AND_ONE_FREE_THROWS = 1, B)
          **ALWAYS 1 — including a made THREE** (§3.12 C:
          3 pts + 1 FT, NOT 3 FTs — do not graduate this)
          +1 if made; FG points already recorded;
        endif
      }
      stop
    else (no)
      :SHOT — MISSED_*;
    endif
  endif
}

partition "Rebounding foul (§3.10 — decisions.md #028)" {
  note right
    **Carved off the TOP of the rebound phase** (C) — rolled BEFORE
    the board contest and SHORT-CIRCUITING it on a hit (the whistle
    stopped play, so nobody rebounds). Same shape as §3.7's block
    carve, which keeps this rate independently tunable — it never
    entangles with the rebound weights.
    **TWO-SIDED** (A2): a defensive box-out push (dominant) or an
    offensive over-the-back (the minority). The committer is drawn
    //foulProne//-weighted from the committing five, so the
    undisciplined bang bodies commit most of them.
    Rate = rareEventProbability(REBOUND_FOUL_BASE, …,
    REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY) × defensivePressure — floor-free,
    its own dial (the PROB_FLOOR trap, #028 impl note).
  end note
  if (rebounding foul?\n//aggregate foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× defensivePressure; REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — REBOUNDING_FOUL_DEFENSE or _OFFENSE
    charge committer foul (feeds foul-outs §3.5)
    committing_team_id = the committing side (#028 D);
    note right
      **EMIT-THEN-COUNT** (A1, the crux): the FOUL event is written
      FIRST, then GameData.isInBonus(committingTeam, period) reads
      the log — so the Nth foul (reaching BONUS_FOULS_PER_PERIOD = 5)
      **itself** sends the fouled team to the line. The penalty is
      **DERIVED from the FOUL events, never stored** — no teamFouls
      field, no reset logic (the #023-F / #013 / #015 discipline).
    end note
    if (**§3.14b — FLAGRANT?**\n//same shared roll (#034 A) — the ONLY site that//\n//can be committed by the OFFENSE (#028 A2, ~22%)//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
      //15% severity sub-roll//; charge committer //recordFoul()//
      on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
      note right
        **The bonus is NOT consulted on a flagrant** — 2 FTs by
        rule, in the penalty or not (the #029 B shape). But the
        flagrant **DOES count toward the period tally** for the
        NEXT foul (#034 I): unlike §3.14a's technical it is a
        personal foul, so ``countsTowardBonus`` excludes it
        **not at all** and neither ``GameData.isInBonus`` nor
        the harness's independent tally changes.
        ⚠ **That non-change is deliberate, not accidental** —
        the exclusion lives in TWO derivations (#032's follow-up).
      end note
      if (DEFENSE committed? //~78%//) then (yes)
        :FREE_THROW ×2 — *_FLAGRANT
        the fouled OFFENSIVE player shoots
        (//foulDrawing//-weighted, #028 B — D)
        → **offense RETAINS** → ``continue`` (B/C)
        //(cap reached ⇒ possession ends, FTs still awarded)//
        **the ``stop`` below means "re-enters the loop", NOT "over"**;
        stop
      else (no — OFFENSE committed, ~22%)
        :FREE_THROW ×2 — *_FLAGRANT
        the fouled DEFENSIVE player shoots
        → **possession FLIPS to the defense** (C)
        → possession over for the offense;
        stop
      endif
    endif
    if (committing team in the bonus?\n//count(FOUL by team, period) >= 5//) then (yes)
      :FREE_THROW ×2 — *_BONUS (source-tagged §3.11 D)
      the FOULED team shoots (foulDrawing-weighted shooter)
      → possession over either way;
      stop
    else (no)
      if (DEFENSE committed?) then (yes)
        :offense was fouled → RETAINS
        → second-chance (respects the off-rebound cap);
        stop
      else (no — offense committed)
        :over-the-back → defense's ball
        → possession over;
        stop
      endif
    endif
  endif
}

partition "MissedShotResolver (§3.8 — #026) — wraps ReboundResolver (§3.3)" {
  note right
    **§3.8 (#026 A/B):** a missed shot resolves to ONE of FOUR
    outcomes in a single SKILL-WEIGHTED draw. MissedShotResolver
    WRAPS ReboundResolver (unchanged) for the rebound-vs-rebound
    balance, then applies a fixed DEFENSE-LEANING lean to carve
    the two OOB slices. NOT a separate "is it OOB?" sub-decision.
    OOB credits NO rebounder (#026 E) and must stay out of the
    rebound reconciliation. Skill-weighted here is the deliberate
    difference from §3.7's FLAT BlockResolver (#026 C).
  end note
  :pick offensive rebounder (offenseRebound draw)
  pick defensive rebounder (defenseRebound draw);
  switch (missed-shot outcome?\n//rebound balance: offenseRebound vs defenseRebound//\n//× fatigueFactor §3.5; OOB slices defense-leaning lean §3.8//\n//(offense-retained forced to ending once cap hit)//)
  case (OFFENSIVE rebound)
    :REBOUND — OFFENSIVE
    credit off rebounder
    → offense retains → second-chance;
    stop
  case (DEFENSIVE rebound)
    :REBOUND — DEFENSIVE
    credit def rebounder
    → possession over;
    stop
  case (OOB — offense §3.8)
    :OUT_OF_BOUNDS_OFFENSE (no rebounder)
    → offense retains → second-chance;
    stop
  case (OOB — defense §3.8)
    :OUT_OF_BOUNDS_DEFENSE (no rebounder)
    → possession over;
    stop
  endswitch
}
repeat while (retentions < MAX_OFFENSIVE_RETENTIONS_PER_POSSESSION?) is (yes) not (no)

:cap reached → next miss forced to DEFENSIVE rebound;
note right
  **The loop has FIVE re-entry paths as of §3.14b** (#034 B):
  offensive rebound (§3.3) · block recovery (§3.7) · OOB-offense
  (§3.8) · rebounding foul (§3.10) · **flagrant retention (§3.14b)**.
  ALL of them count against the ONE cap. **A sixth is the signal
  to restructure this loop** (the #030 clamp-trigger spirit).
  NB the cap bounds FOUR non-rebound paths, which is why it was
  **RENAMED** MAX_OFFENSIVE_REBOUNDS → **MAX_OFFENSIVE_RETENTIONS**
  _PER_POSSESSION (2026-08, post-§3.14b; the loop counter went
  ``offensiveRebounds`` → ``offensiveRetentions`` with it). A pure
  rename — the VALUE is unchanged at 3, and the 5-seed landing
  reproduced byte-for-byte. Do NOT change the value (3→5 is a
  parked idea needing its own recalibration pass — ideas.md).
end note
stop

legend bottom left
  **Probability formula (all resolvers)**
  p = base(path) + SENSITIVITY × (offense − defense) / 10
  Clamped [PROB_FLOOR 0.02, PROB_CEILING 0.97] for
  NORMAL-frequency outcomes (contestProbability).
  Average vs average → base rate. All constants in SimConfig.

  **RARE events use a different clamp** (§3.7 / §3.10 / §3.11)
  rareEventProbability(base, driving, opposing, sensitivity)
  clamps to **[0, ceiling] with NO floor** — on a thin base the
  0.02 floor would act as a FLOOR and make the knob tunable only
  UPWARD (found the hard way in §3.10, #028 impl note). Each rare
  event also carries its OWN sensitivity, far below the global 0.5,
  which would otherwise swamp a thin base: BLOCK_SENSITIVITY 0.12,
  REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY 0.10, AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY 0.10.
  NB a zero base does **not** disable a rare event — the skill term
  alone stays positive off an even contest; only the caller's gate
  truly switches one off. **§3.12 deletes the isContactType gate**,
  so from then on the only off-switch is a **zero foulMultiplier**,
  which scales the whole probability, skill term included (#030 A1).

  **§3.4 coach / chemistry modifiers** (decisions.md #022)
  Each is the avg-10 deviation multiplier
  m(attr) = 1 + COACH_SENSITIVITY × (attr − 10) / 10
  applied as a thumb on the scale over the contest above.

  **§3.5 fatigue / substitution** (decisions.md #023)
  Between-possession sub (top, RNG-free) changes WHO is on
  the floor; each contest skill is × fatigueFactor(energy),
  ×1.0 at a full tank. Minutes are a possession-share
  projection (no game clock). Foul-out = getFouls() >= 6.

  **§3.7 blocked shots** (decisions.md #025)
  BLOCKED? is one leg of a three-way MAKE/MISS/BLOCK draw inside
  ShotResolver (v3): P(BLOCK) carved off the top, defender-vs-
  finisher contest (own BLOCK_SENSITIVITY). A block is a SHOT/
  BLOCKED_* event (a field-goal outcome, exactly as a steal is a
  TURNOVER outcome) — missed FGA on the shooter + a BLK via
  recordBlock() on the defender, no assist. BlockResolver runs a
  flat four-way loose-ball recovery (offense/defense × in-bounds/
  OOB). Recalibrated: ~5 blocks/team, §3.4/§3.5 aggregates held.

  **§3.8 missed-shot OOB** (decisions.md #026)
  A missed shot resolves to ONE of FOUR outcomes in a single
  skill-weighted draw: OFFENSIVE / DEFENSIVE rebound, or OOB
  offense / OOB defense. MissedShotResolver WRAPS ReboundResolver
  (the two-way skill contest, unchanged): it carves the OOB share
  off the top by a flat defense-leaning lean FIRST (skill-
  independent), then runs the board contest only on the clean-
  rebound remainder — NOT a separate OOB sub-decision, so OOB never
  inherits the board winner. Both sail-out (shot flies OOB
  untouched) and tipped-OOB (a board contest, last-touch decides)
  land here, sharing one OOB outcome each (offense/defense). OOB is
  a REBOUND event with an OUT_OF_BOUNDS_* outcome that credits NO
  rebounder and stays out of the rebound reconciliation (#026 E).
  Skill-weighted — the deliberate difference from §3.7's flat
  BlockResolver (#026 C). OOB-offense is a third offense-retention
  path against the one MAX_OFFENSIVE_RETENTIONS cap. Sail-out is a
  new outcome (fewer second chances) → VERIFIED harness-neutral
  (#026 D): OOB ~3/team/game, §3.4/§3.5 aggregates held.

  **§3.9 turnover causes** (decisions.md #027)
  The turnover GATE is untouched — same BASE_TURNOVER, same contest,
  same coach/fatigue scaling — so the turnover COUNT never moves
  (#027 A). A post-declaration weighted draw only picks WHICH of
  nine causes it was, replacing §3.2's binary STOLEN / LOST_BALL.
  STOLEN stays dominant and keeps the pickStealer + recordSteal()
  path; every cause charges the ball-handler. Modest avg-10 leans on
  four causes (#027 C). Note LOST_BALL_OUT_OF_BOUNDS is on TURNOVER
  and must NOT be confused with §3.8's OUT_OF_BOUNDS_* on REBOUND —
  different play types, deliberately distinct vocabulary (#027 D).
  Free by construction → no recalibration.

  **§3.10 rebounding fouls + the team-foul/bonus substrate** (#028)
  A non-shooting foul during the rebound phase, carved off the TOP
  of the board contest and short-circuiting it (C — the §3.7 shape).
  TWO-SIDED (A2): defensive box-out push (dominant) or offensive
  over-the-back, so the committing team is NOT implied by the
  possession orientation — hence game_event.committing_team_id, the
  one additive column this arc took (D). The penalty is **DERIVED**
  from the FOUL log, never stored (A1), emit-then-count so the Nth
  foul awards the bonus itself. Bonus FTs reuse awardFreeThrows
  verbatim (B). NOT free: +2.7 pts before tuning, of which only
  ~1.1 was bonus FTs — **the bigger channel was retained
  possessions**, which the design did not anticipate. BASE_FOUL
  proved the WRONG lever (trimming it RAISES points); the fix was
  the shot BASE_* rates trimmed ~1.2%.

  **§3.11 and-1** (decisions.md #029)
  A defensive foul on a shot that STILL GOES IN: made FG + 1 FT.
  Modeled as a SECOND, post-make foul roll (A1) BESIDE the assist
  (A3) inside SHOT — MADE — the pre-shot foul branch + BASE_FOUL
  are untouched, so the and-1 rate stays independently tunable
  (the §3.7/§3.10 carve, a third time). Scoped to made DRIVE/POST
  (A2 — §3.12 widens to all shot types + fouled-three = 3 FTs).
  Awards exactly ONE FT via a per-situation count through the reused
  awardFreeThrows (B); never forks the possession (the make already
  ended it). Rate = rareEventProbability(AND_ONE_BASE, …,
  AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY) — reuse the machine, own dials, avoiding the
  PROB_FLOOR/global-SENSITIVITY traps §3.7+§3.10 hit (C). Free throws
  become SELF-DESCRIBING (D): each FREE_THROW carries its source
  (SHOOTING / BONUS / AND_ONE), retiring §3.10's accepted ambiguity
  now that there are three FT sources. No schema / OpenAPI / new
  PlayType (AND_ONE is a FOUL outcome, committing_team_id = defTeamId).
  PURE-ADDITIVE points lift → recalibrate the shot BASE_* lever, NOT
  BASE_FOUL (wrong-way, #028 note), by multiple runs to the mean (E).

  **§3.12 all-shot-type contact fouls** (decisions.md #030) **SHIPPED**
  — the two §3.12 notes above mark the forks it changed. The binary ShotType.isContactType() (DRIVE||POST)
  is DELETED (A1) — it gated the WHOLE foul model, so today a jump
  shot cannot be fouled at all. It is replaced by a graduated
